= The Assembly at Weimar

The National Assembly has met in the theatre at Weimar, far from the streets of Berlin, behind a ring of Maercker's volunteers. On 11 February it elected Friedrich Ebert President of the Republic. Philipp Scheidemann leads a coalition of the Social Democrats, the Catholic Centre and the Democrats.

The next day the police arrested Karl Radek in Berlin and took him to Moabit prison. [? if luxemburg_alive = 0 : The same week Jogiches printed a photograph of the Eden Hotel officers celebrating after the murders. The courts showed no interest. ?]
